<script>
  import InstallCommand from "$lib/components/registry/install-command.svelte";
  import { registryConfig } from "$registry/config";
</script>

Before components look correct, add the design system style files. This installs `globals.css` plus the default, secondary, and tertiary theme presets into `styles/` at the project root.

## Prerequisites

Your project should already be set up with [shadcn-svelte](https://www.shadcn-svelte.com/docs/installation) and Tailwind CSS. See [Installation](/docs/installation) for the full setup flow.

## Install

<InstallCommand
  kind="exec"
  args={`shadcn-svelte@latest add ${registryConfig.homepage}/r/styles.json`}
/>

## What gets installed

| File                   | Destination                  |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `globals.css`          | `styles/globals.css`         |
| `theme.css`            | `styles/theme.css`           |
| `theme-secondary.css`  | `styles/theme-secondary.css` |
| `theme-tertiary.css`   | `styles/theme-tertiary.css`  |

The CLI also installs the packages the stylesheet depends on (`tailwindcss`, `tw-animate-css`, and `@fontsource-variable/inter`).

If those files already exist, the CLI may ask before overwriting them.

## Import in your app

Import the globals entry once from your root layout (`src/routes/+layout.svelte`) or app entry:

```svelte
<script>
  import "../../styles/globals.css";
</script>
```

`globals.css` already imports `./theme.css`, `./theme-secondary.css`, and `./theme-tertiary.css`, so you do not need a second import for the theme tokens.

## Theme presets

The published styles are a CSS-first token set for Tailwind v4: a base theme (`theme.css`) plus two alternate presets. Swap the active preset per-page or per-user by setting `data-theme="theme-secondary"` (or `theme-tertiary`) on `<html>`; omit the attribute for the default palette.

```ts
document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "theme-secondary"; // or "theme-tertiary"
```

Each preset only overrides `--primary`, `--ring`, `--sidebar-primary`, `--selection`, and the `--chart-*` scale — everything else (background, foreground, card, border, radius) is shared, so switching presets only changes the accent, not the whole surface.

## Type scale

`theme.css` defines the font-size scale inside `@theme inline`. Tailwind turns each `--text-*` token into a utility of the same name, so `--text-60` is the class `text-60`.

| Utility    | Size  |
| ---------- | ----- |
| `text-10`  | 10px  |
| `text-12`  | 12px  |
| `text-14`  | 14px  |
| `text-16`  | 16px  |
| `text-18`  | 18px  |
| `text-20`  | 20px  |
| `text-24`  | 24px  |
| `text-30`  | 30px  |
| `text-36`  | 36px  |
| `text-48`  | 48px  |
| `text-60`  | 60px  |
| `text-72`  | 72px  |
| `text-96`  | 96px  |
| `text-120` | 120px |

Heading uses the upper end of that scale and steps up at the `sm` breakpoint (640px):

| Size  | Base      | `sm`      |
| ----- | --------- | --------- |
| `xs`  | `text-20` | `text-20` |
| `sm`  | `text-20` | `text-24` |
| `md`  | `text-24` | `text-30` |
| `lg`  | `text-30` | `text-36` |
| `xl`  | `text-36` | `text-48` |
| `2xl` | `text-48` | `text-60` |
| `3xl` | `text-60` | `text-72` |

Text uses the smaller end (`text-12` through `text-20`) and steps up at the same breakpoint.

## Keeping sizes when classes merge

`cn` and `tailwind-variants` know Tailwind's built-in sizes (`text-sm`, `text-xl`). Every other `text-*` class is classified as a text color. A recipe that sets both `text-60` and `text-foreground` loses `text-60` in the merge, and the element keeps the inherited font size. `sm:text-72` lives in its own group, so the larger breakpoint can still apply and the missing size shows up only below `sm`.

This repo registers the scale as font sizes in `registry/items/lib/utils.ts` (`themeTextSizes` and `cnConfig`). `$lib/utils` re-exports that `cn` and `cnConfig`. Pass the same config to every `tv()` recipe that mixes a scale size with a color:

```ts
import { tv } from "tailwind-variants";
import { cnConfig } from "$lib/utils.js";

export const headingVariants = tv(
  {
    variants: {
      size: { md: "text-24 sm:text-30" },
      tone: { default: "text-foreground" },
    },
  },
  { twMergeConfig: cnConfig },
);
```

Add a new size in both places: a `--text-*` custom property in `theme.css`, and the same name in `themeTextSizes`.

